A||||4||Getaway2k||Jack stand question||||5||
Z||000000||Getaway2k||08-20-2000||02:28 PM||||I'm looking for opinions on where the best/safest place to put the jack stands under my Fiero would be. I didn't know if I needed to be concerned with placing them under the frame (and letting the suspension hang) or if I should position them so the suspension is more supported. I can get the stands under the rear (a-frames/control arm?) easily, however, under the front it seems to be easiest placing them under the cross-member (with the wheels hanging). The car will probably be on the stands for several months (throughout the winter).<BR><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://pages.prodigy.net/nuppy/getaway.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-20-2000||04:25 PM||||NEVER put jack stands under the suspension. They always go under solid frame/cradle members. Never lift/tow by suspension parts either.<P>Suspension parts ar not stable and can shift on you resulting in the top of the stand being kicked over. Most of the time they can't take that kind of weight w/o being damaged. Even slight bending will screw them up.<P>Even on vehicles with "solid" rear axles like RWD cars/trucks and FWD mini vans the suspension parts are often not able to take weight directly on them. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||08-20-2000||05:59 PM||||in the middle of a gas tank/fuel pump change now. stands all around on what i guess would be called the frame rails. not sure if thats what they're considered to be on a fiero. i used ramps the last time i did this but this car dosen't run.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||08-20-2000||11:48 PM||||I usually put mine under the rear cradle side rails, centered in between the control arm bolts.  I lift from the center of the rear cradle crossmember.  <BR>While I had the cradle out, I put the stands just forward of the front cradle mounts, with 1X4 boards going forward, so I wouldn't dimple the floorpan.<BR>In front, I lift from the center of the front crossmember and put the jackstands right near the ends of it. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||08-21-2000||07:02 AM||||in the rear, between the front cradle mount and the suspension... i jack from one side to the other.<P>in the front, i jack from the middle of the crossmember and put a jack stand on the ends... trick here is that the beam is not straight, the right side has a slight rise.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
